 "intro": "A camp kitchen has three serious risks: fire, carbon monoxide and bad water or food. All three are avoidable with a few habits learned before you leave home. This module covers how to run a stove safely, why you never cook or burn anything in a closed tent, how to make water safe, and how to keep food cold enough and cooked enough. Lecturer lens: Fridtjof Nansen weighed fuel, food and cooking gear as carefully as anything. His account of the cooker and its tests is a worked example of choosing a stove from numbers.",
