     "x": "In Ireland, electronic direct marketing by phone, fax, text and email is covered by the GDPR and by the ePrivacy Regulations (SI 336 of 2011). {{dpc-faq}} The Data Protection Commission's guidance covers when consent is required, a limited exception for existing customers if specific requirements such as a clear opt-out are met, and how people can object. {{dpc-faq}} We read only the summary page, not the full guidance PDF, so use the DPC page itself for details. Irish consumer law also bans persistent unwanted offers. {{ci-unfair}}"
