 "intro": "Most people are nervous about speaking to a group, and most people will have to do it. This module explains what public speaking is for, why honesty and credit for sources matter, what nerves really are, and a set of practical ways to manage them. By the end you will have a plan for your own nerves, not just a hope that they go away. Lecturer lens: Aristotle's Rhetoric starts by asking what a speaker can actually do to persuade. His answer gives you a short audit for any speech: who decides, about what, and by which of three means.",
