      "Take a short budget pitch of 24 sentences. Label each sentence by its main job: argument and evidence, credibility of the speaker, or feeling of the audience.",
      "Suppose the count is 14 argument, 6 credibility and 4 feeling. That is 58 percent, 25 percent and 17 percent. Aristotle gives no proportions, so these are our adaptation, not his rule. {{arist-b1}}",
      "Check each group against his tests. Argument: could the proof stand if the speaker were unknown? Credibility: is it shown by what is said, and not by a title? Feeling: is the feeling about the matter, or a lever to avoid the facts? {{arist-b1}}",
      "Because the pitch is political, the end is the expedient: does every sentence help show that the plan will do good? {{arist-b1}}",
      "Strike or rewrite any sentence that fails its test, then recount."
