 "intro": "A speech is for someone. Before you write a word you need to know who will listen, what they care about, and exactly what you want the speech to do. This module covers how listening works, how to learn about an audience without stereotyping it, how to choose and narrow a topic, and how to write a clear purpose statement. Lecturer lens: Aristotle describes how age and fortune shape what people feel and want, and tells speakers to adapt to them. His sorting is a starting list of questions, not a set of facts about your audience.",
