 "intro": "A speech that is only opinion is easy to ignore. This module covers how to plan research time, find and judge sources, choose the right kind of support for each point, and present evidence honestly and clearly in speech. It also covers how to cite aloud so that no one can mistake your voice for someone else's. Lecturer lens: Cicero's De oratore is a dialogue about what it takes to be an orator. It gives a five-part plan for preparing a speech and a memory method that works by imagined places and images.",
