 "intro": "A programme only works if the client keeps going. This module uses the evidence on autonomous motivation and motivational interviewing, and a three-level goal structure, to turn a plan into a habit. Lecturer lens: Carl Rogers' 1957 paper is short, and its six conditions are stated as a hypothesis for psychotherapy. It also says things a trainer must not copy, such as that no diagnosis is needed. Reading the paper itself shows what to borrow and what to leave.",
