     "x": "Britannica adds that the American Method was Lee Strasberg's adaptation, which encouraged actors to use their own emotional memory. {{brit-stan}} Stanislavski himself kept changing his approach for forty years, and in 1935 he began a final technique he called the method of physical actions. {{brit-stan}} For directing, our inference is to follow the book's order: set the circumstances, ask the question, then ask for an action."
