     "x": "The book warns against dividing a play into hundreds of tiny steps, because the actor then loses the whole. {{aap}} Divide for preparation, then let the pieces fuse into large units during performance. {{aap}} The test for what to keep is simple: what is the core of the play, the part without which it cannot exist? {{aap}}"
