     "t": "p",
     "x": "Acting began on the stage, and the first screen actors carried the stage habit of playing big for the back row. {{cwc}} The camera was far more intimate than anyone expected, so the style slowly shrank to suit it. {{cwc}} The textbook also says that the theatrical style of early films worked for the audiences of the time, because they knew nothing else. {{cwc}}"
