 "intro": "Once each actor has a world and an objective, the next job is to connect the actors to each other and to the whole play. This module covers communion and adaptation between actors, the through-line and super-objective, and how to run the rehearsal room and give notes. The last lesson takes the same ideas onto a film set. Lecturer lens: Stanislavski said an actor has no real line until the pieces join. The book gives the 'day backwards' exercise for building each actor's line, and a chapter that shows how all the small objectives should pull toward one super-objective.",
