 "intro": "A play is performed in a place, for a particular audience, with a team and a budget. This module covers the three common stage layouts, the empty-space idea, designers and budgets, and the last weeks before opening. Each lesson also notes what changes on a screen production. Lecturer lens: Brook began from a bare space and a watching audience. We could not read The Empty Space, so this lesson uses Britannica, Wikipedia and the Royal Shakespeare Company's page on the 1970 Dream, and says so.",
