      "Revenue: 60 seats at $10 for each of 5 nights, if every seat sold, is 60 x $10 x 5 = $3,000. At half full it is $1,500, still above $870. At a quarter full it is 15 x $10 x 5 = $750, which is below $870.",
      "Break-even: $870 / ($10 x 5 nights) = 17.4, so you need 18 seats a night, which is 30 percent of the house."
